+# Hegel Property-Based Testing Report: ciborium
+
+Property-based tests were added to the `ciborium` package using
+[hegel](https://hegel.dev) (`hegeltest` 0.28.2, added with
+`--ignore-rust-version`: the crate pins `rust-version = 1.85`, hegeltest
+requires 1.86 — a dev-dependency-only concern).
+
+Shared generators live in `ciborium/tests/common/mod.rs`: a recursive
+`Value` generator (integers over the full encodable `[-2^64, 2^64-1]` range
+with boosted width boundaries, floats including arbitrary bit patterns /
+NaN payloads, bytes, text, bools, null, tags, arrays, maps), configurable
+to exclude bignum tags 2/3, tag map keys, or duplicate map keys. Floats are
+compared bitwise (`eqv`) so NaN roundtrips are judged fairly.
+
+## Properties tested
+
+| # | Property | File | Evidence |
+|---|----------|------|----------|
+| 1 | `Value` -> bytes -> `Value` roundtrip (tags 2/3 excluded) | `tests/codec.rs::props::value_bytes_roundtrip` | Crate-level roundtrip promise; the existing rstest matrix checks it for fixed cases. Tags 2/3 excluded because ciborium intentionally decodes bignums into `Value::Integer`/normalized bytes (the "Not In RFC" rstest cases). |
+| 2 | `Value::serialized` / `Value::deserialized` are the identity on `Value` (all tags incl. 2/3) | `tests/codec.rs::props::value_serializer_is_identity` | The rstest matrix asserts `Value::serialized(&input)` equals the expected `Value` for every case. |
+| 3 | Serde-derived struct/enum roundtrips via byte path and dynamic `Value` path | `tests/codec.rs::props::derived_types_roundtrip` | Existing cases for `UnitStruct`/`TupleStruct`/`Enum`; generalized to generated field values (u64, String, Vec<u8>, char, Vec<String>, enum with all variant shapes, Option, HashMap, tuple). |
+| 4 | Full-range `i128` roundtrip (plain + bignum encodings, `-(2^64)` boundary, `i128::MIN/MAX`) | `tests/codec.rs::props::i128_bytes_roundtrip` | rstest cases for `±18446744073709551616i128` etc.; `src/ser/mod.rs::serialize_i128` / `src/de/mod.rs::integer`. |
+| 5 | Full-range `u128` roundtrip (bignum tag 2 above `u64::MAX`, `u128::MAX`) | `tests/codec.rs::props::u128_bytes_roundtrip` | Same as above for the unsigned path. |
